{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Mei, sorry you're having trouble. I'd like to help, but I need a bit more detail first. Could you tell me: (1) what isn't working (for example email, Teams, printing, signing in, an app, or your Mac), (2) what happens when you try, including the exact wording of any error message (a screenshot is great), and (3) when it started? One thing I noticed while checking: your mailbox is almost completely full (over 99%). If your problem is with email, such as messages not sending, Outlook not syncing, or 'mailbox full' warnings, that's probably the cause. You can free up space by emptying Deleted Items and Junk Email, sorting your Inbox and Sent Items by size, and deleting large attachments or saving them to OneDrive. Reply with the details and I'll take it from there.",
  "internal_note": "The ticket gave no details ('it's not working'). Checked: account is active, not locked (0 failed sign-ins), sign-in not blocked, VPN enabled, no forced password change. Laptop BL-LT-0109 (macOS 15) is online with a recent check-in, 14.6% disk free, and no warnings. Notable finding: the mailbox is at 99.4% (50890/51200 MB). Per KB-010, sending stops at 100%, so this is the likeliest cause if the problem is email. I gave the user the KB-010 cleanup steps as a possible fix and asked what's failing, any error message, and when it started. I haven't confirmed the actual problem, so no fix actions were queued.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-010"
  ],
  "confidence": "low"
}
